
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Whisper Memos just <a href="https://whispermemos.com/changelog/2026-09-mcp">added an MCP server</a>, and I am already digging it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;ve written before about how much I like <a href="https://wisprflow.ai/r?WISPR34511">Wispr Flow</a>. I use it frequently on my Mac. But there is another transcription tool on my belt. Whisper Memos is my choice when I am mobile. (Whisper Memos has sponsored MacSparky in the past, but I was a paying subscriber long before that.)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;ve got Whisper Memos connected to Drafts so I can press the Action button on my watch or phone, say a few words, and in about a minute they show up in my Drafts Inbox. It does a good job of capturing my voice, and I don&#8217;t have to stop what I am doing to type. I use this workflow multiple times a day.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Whisper Memos got some recent updates that are of note and will simplify this workflow. First, there is a small new Apple Watch feature I like. The watch now shows a live timer while it records. That little bit of feedback is helpful. I can glance down and know everything is still working.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The MCP connection is the bigger update. Once connected, an AI assistant can read your Whisper Memos transcripts, summaries, and labels when you ask. The connection is read-only. The assistant cannot listen to the audio, edit a memo, or delete one.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I have set up a simple protocol. If I want my assistant to act on a recording, I begin by saying, &#8220;This is for ChatGPT&#8221; or &#8220;This is for Claude.&#8221; Later, I ask it to look in Whisper Memos and take it from there.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I have not decided whether I will automate that handoff or leave it on demand. For now, I like being able to press the Action Button on my Apple Watch, speak a few instructions, and know I can hand the recording to my assistant later.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This post is a good example. I dictated it into my watch while sitting in a comfortable chair in my backyard.</p>
